As you pause to take in the full majesty of your surroundings, you realize 
that this may in fact be the loneliest place in all the world.  The tall 
stone monuments of an age long past stand as a monument to what once took place
here, long before the dawn of O'len. The carvings are worn, but still stand
out in defiance of the passage of time. They are in a language that you do not
understand, but the simple reliefs show the history of the sundering of the
divines, of the sleep of Casimir, of the births of Ruotsalainen, and of the
coming of the divines into O'len. The ground itself seems to quail in protest
of your footsteps and it is clear to you that yours may be the first feet, 
divine or mortal, to tread here in an age. The wind howls low through the 
stone towers of old as you consider the paths that lie before you.
